<header class="hero"><p class="eyebrow">myColorado / Digital identity</p><h1>Mobile driver’s license</h1><p class="deck">Helping a long-running initiative move forward, from stalled work to launch.</p></header>
<section class="launch-panel" aria-labelledby="launch-title"><div><p class="eyebrow">Shipped / myColorado mDL</p><h2 id="launch-title">A new way through airport security.</h2></div><div><p>Our team launched a mobile driver’s license you can use at TSA.</p><a href="https://www.tsa.gov/news/press/releases/2026/08/31/tsa-accepts-mycolorado-mdls-during-identity-verification" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read the TSA announcement <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span><span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a></div></section>
<section class="chapter" aria-labelledby="context-title"><h2 id="context-title">The context</h2><div class="chapter-copy"><p class="lead">This initiative sits within my broader work leading design across myColorado.</p><p>The mobile driver’s license had been a long-running effort. I helped our team unblock the work and bring it to launch, while continuing to work across the wider product and its design system.</p><dl class="facts"><div><dt>My role</dt><dd>Design lead</dd></div><div><dt>Product</dt><dd>myColorado</dd></div><div><dt>Focus</dt><dd>Digital identity</dd></div></dl></div></section>
<section class="chapter" aria-labelledby="launch-story-title"><h2 id="launch-story-title">The launch</h2><div class="chapter-copy"><p>Our team’s work brought the mobile driver’s license to TSA identity verification. I was invited to DIA with the team for the governor’s announcement.</p><p><a href="https://x.com/GovofCO/status/2094562971292762554" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">See the announcement <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span><span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a></p></div></section>
